  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Skies are partly to mostly sunny this\nafternoon across northern and central Nevada. Isolated, weak echos\ncan be seen across portions of northeast Elko county. No lightning\nstrikes have been detected yet. Winds are breezy with general \ngusts of 30 mph observed. Look for the clouds to gradually \ndiminish during the overnight period with winds decreasing as \nwell. Low temperatures tonight will be in the 30s and 40s.\n\nLarge upper low will be centered across the northern portion of \nthe United States with an upper ridge over the eastern Pacific \nOcean. This will keep a northwest flow aloft across the forecast \narea on Wednesday. Skies will be mainly sunny across the region \nwith highs in the 70s and 80s. Winds will be breezy out of the \nnorthwest with sustained winds of 15 to 25 mph and gusts of 30 to \n35 mph. Quiet weather with light winds are expected overnight with\nlows in the 30s and 40s. Because of the light winds and drier \nair, some locations in Elko county will see lows around freezing \nby Thursday morning and could affect temperature sensitive plants.\n\nFriday through Tuesday, conditions are expected to remain on the \ndry side with general afternoon breeziness. High temperatures will\nbe in the 80s with lows in the 30s and 40s Thursday night into \nFriday. The warm-up continues Friday through the weekend with \nafternoon high temperatures warming into the 80s and 90s with lows\nin the 40s and 50s.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: Minor updates to the PoP, \nweather, wind and wind gust grids were made in the short term due \nto concerns with fire weather. Otherwise no changes were made. \nConfidence is high in the upcoming dry conditions and warming \ntemperatures that are expected to last through the weekend.",
